SERIALIZATION - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

serialization.serialize(value[, pretty]) -> string

Turns a value (nil, boolean, number, string, or
tables of those) into Lua source text. Tables with
cycles raise an error. pretty = true adds line
breaks and indentation, and shows other values
(functions) as names instead of failing.

serialization.unserialize(text) -> value

Reads text made by serialize back into a value.
Returns nil, reason for invalid text. The text
can't run code.

  filesystem.writeAll("/home/cfg", serialization.serialize({volume = 3, names = {"a", "b"}}))
  local cfg = serialization.unserialize(filesystem.readAll("/home/cfg"))
